// items[].cost is the LINE total (unit price × quantity), per the manual test case's
// framing of "the specific bug class a multi-quantity order is meant to expose." That
// assertion failed against the real app — the checkout API's `cost` field is the UNIT
// price, unmultiplied, regardless of quantity. It's the frontend's own order-confirmation
// page (pages/cart/checkout/[orderId]/index.tsx) that multiplies cost × quantity
// client-side to compute what it displays as the line total. So the API contract itself
// doesn't carry a "line total" field at all — the multiplication is a presentation-layer
// concern, not something this API-level test can assert on. What IS API-testable, and
// is asserted below: quantity is correct per line, and the unit cost for a multi-quantity
// line matches the same product's unit price from GET /api/products (i.e. not silently
// divided/altered because the quantity happens to be > 1).
const qty3Line = order.items.find((i: any) => i.item.productId === PRODUCT_IDS.TRAVEL_TELESCOPE);
